 "eras": [
  {"id":"1667","year":"1667","label":"Completed by Shivaji","short":"1667","lens":"none","summary":"The island fort at Kurte, built from 1664 and finished in 1667, shown as the later chart and the present coast draw it.","basis":"Wikipedia: foundation 25 November 1664, built 1664-67, Hiroji Indulkar chief architect, 48 acres (SIN-16 for the tourism description). The drawn outline is the 1765 chart carried back 98 years, marked inferred.","conjecture":"No plan of 1667 was found. The island rim and the 1765 wall line are carried back unchanged; any later change to the walls or buildings is not known.","sources":["SIN-02","SIN-16"],"facts":["Construction started on 25 November 1664 and ran to 1667 (Wikipedia, which flags other claims on the page as needing citations).","Hiroji Indulkar is named chief architect; Shivaji reportedly brought 200 Vaddera workers (Wikipedia)."]},
  {"id":"1765","year":"1765","label":"Watson's survey","short":"Fort Augustus","lens":"engraving","summary":"The fort as surveyed by Co. John Watson in 1765, labelled \"Sinderdroo, or Fort Augustus\", and published by Dalrymple in 1774.","basis":"The chart \"View and plan of Sinderdroo or Melundy, on the Malabar coast\", registered to OSM by fitting the island silhouette only (IoU 0.91). The chart's printed scale bar agrees with the fitted scale to 8%.","conjecture":"It is a hydrographic chart: the fort is about 1 cm across, the wall is a hatched line, and no bastion, gate, height or thickness can be read. About 30 small blocks and houses are drawn that are not traced.","sources":["SIN-02","SIN-16"],"facts":["The chart legend: A. \"Sinderdroo, or Fort Augustus\", a. \"Cavalier, & Flag on D°\", B. Pudendroo, C. Rajacoote Fort.","Imprint: published according to Act of Parliament by A. Dalrymple, 25 July 1774; the survey is dated 1765."]},
  {"id":"today","year":"Today","label":"ASI monument","short":"Monument","lens":"none","summary":"A protected monument on Kurte island off Malvan, reached by boat, with a few families still living inside.","basis":"The OSM island coastline, two short wall fragments and about 20 buildings and tracks, plus the wall line, cavalier and blocks traced from the 1765 chart.","conjecture":"The chart elements are 1765 positions with the registration error above; whether each survives is not checked. Heights are unknown (kerb-high) in this evidence layer; see the constructed layer.","sources":["SIN-02","SIN-16","MMI-06"],"facts":["Protected monument under the Archaeological Survey of India; closed to tourists in the rains because of high tides (Wikipedia, both marked as needing citations).","Inscribed in 2025 as a component of \"Maratha Military Landscapes of India\" (Wikipedia; SIN-12..15 are the dossier, not reusable here)."]}
 ],
